{
  "id": "close-pending-split-then-split",
  "priority": "P0",
  "title": "P0 STATUS 1584: from a terminal, in one burst: Cmd-D, a line typed at once, Cmd-W, Cmd-D, a line typed at once. Cmd-W closes the pending split; the second Cmd-D makes a new pane that gets the focus and runs the second line",
  "why": "STATUS 1584 (found by the P0 1193 owner on feat bcec3ce42ba): Cmd-W cancelled the pending split, but the window kept the closed stand-in and the focus on its pane id until its store observation ran a turn later. A second Cmd-D in that window split the closed stand-in, which no daemon pane takes over, and made NO pane. Fix: fix/p0-close-pending-split-focus (the window applies the store in the close's own turn; the focus goes to the pane the split was made from). Expected: base FAIL (no second pane, or d2 not in a new pane), fix head PASS.",
  "source": "Packages/macOS/CmuxNext/Tests/CmuxNextAppTests/ClosedPendingSplitFocusTests.swift (same burst, in-process)",
  "budget_seconds": 150,
  "steps": [
    {
      "do": "smoke_ready",
      "timeout": 60
    },
    {
      "do": "smoke_remember_workspaces"
    },
    {
      "do": "smoke_make_key"
    },
    {
      "do": "smoke_snapshot",
      "name": "before_terminal"
    },
    {
      "do": "key",
      "key": "n",
      "modifiers": [
        "cmd"
      ],
      "mark": "ws1"
    },
    {
      "do": "expect",
      "title": "Cmd-N makes a workspace (the frame kept: not blank)",
      "since": "ws1",
      "timeout": 20,
      "all": [
        {
          "smoke_workspaces": {
            "new": 1
          }
        },
        {
          "smoke_frame": {}
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "do": "key",
      "key": "`",
      "modifiers": [
        "control"
      ],
      "mark": "wsterm1"
    },
    {
      "do": "smoke_type_now",
      "text": "echo s0-${nonce}-$((6*7))"
    },
    {
      "do": "expect",
      "title": "the workspace's Ctrl-` terminal ran its line and has the focus: the burst starts from a terminal",
      "since": "wsterm1",
      "timeout": 30,
      "all": [
        {
          "smoke_new_terminals": {
            "since": "before_terminal",
            "lines": [
              "s0-${nonce}-42"
            ],
            "focused": "s0-${nonce}-42",
            "placement": "new_workspaces"
          }
        },
        {
          "smoke_key_window": {}
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "do": "smoke_snapshot",
      "name": "before_splits"
    },
    {
      "do": "key",
      "key": "d",
      "modifiers": [
        "cmd"
      ],
      "mark": "split1"
    },
    {
      "do": "smoke_type_now",
      "text": "echo d1-${nonce}-$((6*7))"
    },
    {
      "do": "key",
      "key": "w",
      "modifiers": [
        "cmd"
      ],
      "mark": "close1"
    },
    {
      "do": "key",
      "key": "d",
      "modifiers": [
        "cmd"
      ],
      "mark": "split2"
    },
    {
      "do": "smoke_type_now",
      "text": "echo d2-${nonce}-$((6*7))"
    },
    {
      "do": "expect",
      "title": "Cmd-D, line, Cmd-W, Cmd-D, line: the closed split stays closed; the second Cmd-D made one new pane, it has the focus and ran the second line; the first line ran nowhere",
      "since": "split1",
      "timeout": 30,
      "all": [
        {
          "smoke_panes": {
            "line": "d2-${nonce}-42",
            "count": 2
          }
        },
        {
          "smoke_new_terminals": {
            "since": "before_splits",
            "lines": [
              "d2-${nonce}-42"
            ],
            "focused": "d2-${nonce}-42",
            "placement": "new_panes"
          }
        },
        {
          "smoke_app_lines": {
            "lines": [
              "s0-${nonce}-42",
              "d2-${nonce}-42"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "smoke_key_window": {}
        },
        {
          "frame_screen": {
            "shows": [
              "d2-${nonce}-42"
            ],
            "lacks": [
              "d1-${nonce}-42"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "do": "smoke_no_key_gaps"
    }
  ],
  "finally": [
    {
      "do": "smoke_close_all"
    }
  ]
}
